From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vadim Kochan <vadim4j@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 04:05:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: tegra-pkvm: use translated DMA domains by default

Do not force every Tegra device into an identity IOMMU domain.  Devices
whose DMA mask is smaller than physical memory need an IOVA aperture so
the DMA API can map high pages into an address the device can reach.

In particular, SDMMC uses a 34-bit DMA aperture on AGX Orin.  With an
identity domain, allocations above 16 GiB fail DMA mapping and the SDHCI
controller receives the masked DMA_MAPPING_ERROR value 0x3ffffff00,
which falls in VPR and prevents the eMMC from being read.

Return no device-specific override and let the IOMMU core select its
normal translated DMA domain.  The Tegra pKVM frontend already implements
paging-domain allocation, mapping, unmapping, and attachment.

Signed-off-by: Vadim Kochan <vadim4j@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c b/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
index 41fa98341045..8088b3a32324 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
@@ -314,7 +314,7 @@ static struct iommu_domain *pkvm_tegra_domain_alloc_paging(struct device *dev)
 
 static int pkvm_tegra_default_domain(struct device *dev)
 {
-	return IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDENTITY;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static const struct iommu_ops pkvm_tegra_iommu_ops = {
